# Welcome!

#### This professional learning module prepares you to teach **The Fabric of the Internet and AI**—a unit which explores the Internet's function (data transmission, addressing, security, protocols), its societal/ethical impacts (like the digital divide), and how AI is used in cybersecurity, preparing students to propose solutions for access and security.

___

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 95%; margin: 20pt auto; padding: 0 5px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/36211eedb3698751fa5523b4dde93351-image-1760467094025.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/7f813b0aec7d472e470f94eb91471aa1-image-1760466945803.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/ddb463a06ccc88f5d7390a1f841a0f31-image-1760467013014.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
</div>

___


#### **By the end of this professional learning module, you will be able to:**

* #### Prepare to teach foundational Internet concepts by guiding students through the structure and function of key network components, including routers, IP addresses, and data routing.

* #### Support students in developing a deep understanding of how the Internet works by using the Internet Simulator to model packets, protocols, and communication across networks.

* #### Lead students in analyzing issues of digital access and equity as they design an Internet Access Advocacy Campaign that blends technical understanding with real-world social impact.

* #### Guide students in exploring network security principles by examining common vulnerabilities, simulating attacks, and evaluating strategies that protect data and ensure safe communication online.


## Take Our Pre-Survey

#### To better gauge your learning and improve this professional learning module, please take our pre-survey - it will take fewer than five minutes to complete.

<div style="margin: 20px 0px">
<a class="btn btn-large btn-primary" href="google.com" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Take the Pre-Survey</a>
</div>

### **Suggested total time for this module:** 60 minutes




 


